========================================================================
1. Well-defined symbol (no implicit decl / missing symbol)
========================================================================

### Product host — PASS

| Probe | Result |
|-------|--------|
| `strings` | `c_guard_scan_idents` present |
| `nm -S --defined-only` | `000000000045fb90 00000000000014ea T c_guard_scan_idents` |
| `readelf -s` | FUNC GLOBAL DEFAULT, size **5354** |
| Undefined in host? | **no** `U c_guard_scan_idents` |
| `c_secret_emit_guard` (4738 B) | **1** direct `call c_guard_scan_idents` |

5354 bytes is a full walker, not a stub. Inlined refuse path inside the scan (gcc -O2): `c_secret_resolve_alias`×1 + `c_secret_refuse_sink_ident`×1 (matches `.oo` `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` body).

### Emit-time declaration order — PASS

`.oo` order (helpers first):

1. `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`
2. `c_guard_scan_idents`
3. `c_secret_emit_guard` → sole source call site

Product `cli_emit.oo` default `emit-c` (no `EMIT_NO_CONCAT`): `c_emit_stream_mode(src, "protos")` then `"bodies"`. `c_emit_fn_mode(..., "protos")` prints `ret name(args);` for every non-`main` fn.

Live emit of the guard module (failed later on the body — §3) **did** print, before any `{`:

```
void c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(OoStr env, OoStr t, OoStr name);
void c_guard_scan_idents(OoStr env, OoStr sink, OoStr args);
void c_secret_emit_guard(OoStr env, OoStr t, OoStr a0, OoStr a1, OoStr a2, OoStr args);
```

`oodac_test_build.tmp.c` L550 still holds the same proto (protos-only artifact).

`oodac_pure_build.sh` extracts `ret name(args);` from the first `ret name(args) {` per symbol and concatenates **preamble + protos + bodies** — so even per-file `all` emit is re-prototyped before link.

Single-pass `all` without that extract still sees a **definition** of `c_guard_scan_idents` before `c_secret_emit_guard` calls it (helper-before-callee). Comment in `.oo` updated this pass: that order is belt-and-suspenders, not the product proto mechanism.

### Implicit-decl contrast — PASS (mechanism)

| TU | `gcc -std=c11 -Werror=implicit-function-declaration` |
|----|------------------------------------------------------|
| proto present, take address of `c_guard_scan_idents` | **PROBE_COMPILE_OK** |
| call with **no** proto | **error** (implicit declaration of `c_guard_scan_idents`) |

Product TU shape is the first row (protos pass). Missing-symbol link fail is what t1_memory M-SG1 recorded when the walker had call sites and **no** body; that hole is closed on this ELF.

========================================================================
2. No leftover stack buffer / fixed char[N] in C emit of this walk
========================================================================

### Source (.oo) — PASS

`c_guard_scan_idents` (after comment-only honesty):

- Ident extract: `let name = str_slice(args, start, i);` then `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`.
- **No** `name = name + char_at`.
- **No** `char buf[N]` / `char ident[...]` (language has no stack `char[]` in `.oo`).

SPRINT “stack buffer” wording = do not cap the ident in a fixed C array **and** do not rebuild it char-by-char. Alpha close = **one slice per span** (`t1_memory.oot` M-SG1/M-SG2; rollup ALREADY_FIXED).

### Product machine code — PASS

`objdump` of `c_guard_scan_idents` (5354 B):

| Callee | Count | Role |
|--------|------:|------|
| `oo_str_lit` | 127 | letter / digit / punct tables |
| `oo_str_eq` | 127 | same |
| `oo_str_release` | 7 | stored `OoStr` temps |
| `oo_char_at` | 6 | classification + comment skip |
| `oo_chars_len` | 1 | `n` |
| `oo_str_slice` | 1 | **the ident** |
| `c_secret_resolve_alias` | 1 | refuse (inlined helper) |
| `c_secret_refuse_sink_ident` | 1 | refuse |

- **Zero** `sprintf` / `strncpy`.
- Entry: `sub $0x98, %rsp` — 152-byte spill frame for `OoStr` pairs + callee-saves, **not** a `char ident[N]`.
- `char` text in the dump is only `oo_char_at` / `oo_chars_len` names.

### Floor (chs_rt, not primary) — note only

`runtime/chs_rt_str.c`:

- `oo_char_at` — heap 1-char (or UTF-8 1–4 byte) `OoStr` via `oo_str_alloc_payload`.
- `oo_str_slice` — heap copy of the `[start,end)` span (O(|ident|)), fail-soft empty on OOB.

These are the **runtime** implementations the emitted walk calls. There is **no** `c_guard_scan_idents` in `chs_rt*.c` / `chs_rt.h`.

### Unreclaimed temps (residual, not 7.1 CRIT)

Emitted (and `.oo`) block-comment skip uses **inline** `char_at(args, i)` / `char_at(args, i+1)` inside `oo_str_eq(...)` — product shows those as 2 of the 6 `oo_char_at` sites. Stored `c` / `n1` / `d` are `oo_str_release`d. Inline results are not. O(n) leak on `/* */` spans in **arg text**, not a stack overflow and not per-char ident concat.

========================================================================
3. Re-emit residual (current host vs this .oo)
========================================================================

Live (this pass):

```
ooda/oodac/oodac emit-c ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo
```

- Prints preamble + **three protos** + complete `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` + start of `c_guard_scan_idents`.
- Dies at the untyped `let is_start = c == "_" || c == "a" || …` chain:

```
ERR	c_emit	unknown free call needs annotation	oo_str_eq
```

Gate: `c_emit_let_ext.oo` `c_emit_let_untyped_ty` — `c_rhs_call_name` sees lowered `oo_str_eq(...)` and `oo_str_eq` is **not** on the String/Int allowlist → `process_exit(1)`.

`if c == "\""` earlier in the same fn **does** emit (`if` is not an untyped `let`). Same failure with `EMIT_NO_CONCAT=1`.

Honesty: **this host cannot re-emit its own walker**. The shipping ELF was produced by a prior emit that accepted the same giant `||` as `long long`. Rebuild of oodac from **this** `.oo` on **this** host will fail-closed (ERR line / emit abort), not silently drop the symbol.

Out of scope this auditor (comment-only): annotate `let is_start: Bool` / `let is_cont: Bool`, or allowlist `oo_str_eq` as Int, or use `char_is_alpha` / `char_is_digit` (preamble already declares them).

